<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cenél Conaill</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cenel Conaill</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cenél Conaill were a kindred of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conall-gulban">Conall Gulban</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niall-of-the-nine-hostages">Niall of the Nine Hostages</a>, and based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">Tír Chonaill</a>, modern County Donegal. Saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba</a> belonged to them. They shared the high kingship with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-neogain">Cenél nEógain</a> until the 8th century, and their later leading family, the O'Donnells, ruled Tír Chonaill until 1607.</p></div>
